    "problem_statement": "# Functions with keyword-only arguments fail to unpickle correctly\n\n## Describe the bug\n\nWhen using cloudpickle to pickle and unpickle functions with keyword-only arguments, the unpickled function fails with a TypeError indicating a missing required keyword-only argument.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport cloudpickle\n\ndef example(a, *, _):\n    return a\n\n# Pickle the function\npickled = cloudpickle.dumps(example)\n\n# Unpickle the function\nunpickled = cloudpickle.loads(pickled)\n\n# Try to call the unpickled function\nunpickled(1)  # This should work but fails\n```\n\n## Expected Results\n\nThe unpickled function should work exactly like the original function, accepting the same arguments.\n\n## Actual Results\n\n```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\nTypeError: example() missing 1 required keyword-only argument: '_'\n```\n\nThe unpickled function seems to have incorrect argument specifications, requiring an additional keyword-only argument that wasn't required in the original function.\n\n## Additional Information\n\nThis issue appears to be related to how code objects are serialized and reconstructed. The problem specifically affects functions with keyword-only arguments, but may also impact other function types.\n\nI've also noticed that the issue is consistent across different pickle protocols.\n\n## Versions\n\n```\nPython: 3.10.15\ncloudpickle: latest\n```"
